Found by langertha-llm-advisor during core k238 design pass (2026-09-25), code-read only, not run.

Knarr::Router::_engine_cache_key is join("|", engine, url, api_key_env) — the model is not part of it. _get_engine sets $args{model} only when constructing, so the second configured (or auto-discovered) model on the same engine/url/key gets the CACHED instance built for the first model. Request::chat_f_args passes no model, so the upstream body carries the first model (chat_model is ro), and Handler::Router then clone_with(model => $canonical_model) — the client sees the model it asked for while another model answered.

Also wrong per model: every model-scoped decision in core (layer-3 model_capability_corrections, model_capability_exclusions, Reasoning::Profile, and the proposed model-aware tool_wire_format of core k238) is evaluated for the wrong chat_model.

Worst case: auto_discover on a gateway (OpenRouter, NousResearch, HuggingFace) — all discovered slugs collapse onto one model.

Fix direction: include the resolved model in the cache key (or cache per engine config and clone with chat_model => $model per resolved model). Test: two models, same engine/url/key, assert two distinct chat_model on the upstream request.
